---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What SmallNestDecor is, who it is for, and how we choose the ideas we publish.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-terracotta-dark">Hello, small home</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">About SmallNestDecor</h1>

    <div class="prose-nest mt-8">
      <p>
        SmallNestDecor exists for one simple reason: most decor advice is written for
        houses, with spare rooms, renovation budgets, and walls you are allowed to
        drill into. We write for the rest of us. Our readers live in studios,
        one-bedroom apartments, first small homes, and rentals where the lease says
        no in three different places.
      </p>
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        If you have ever measured a sofa against an elevator door, stored the
        suitcases under the bed, or wondered which white paint will not turn your
        north-facing living room blue, you are our people. Our ideas assume real
        floor plans, real budgets, and usually a landlord.
      </p>
      <h2>How we choose ideas</h2>
      <p>
        Every guide on SmallNestDecor has to pass three tests. Does it work in a
        genuinely small space, not a "small" showroom? Can it be done without
        permanent changes, or is the permanent part honestly flagged? And would we
        spend our own money on it, in that order? Ideas that fail a test do not get
        published, however pretty they are.
      </p>
      <h2>A note on our images</h2>
      <p>
        Many of the rooms you will see here are <strong>AI-generated inspiration
        renders</strong>, created to show a color, a layout, or a mood as clearly as
        possible. They are illustrations of ideas, not photographs of real homes,
        and never a promise that a specific product looks a certain way. Where a
        guide depends on a real product, we say so and link to the retailer so you
        can judge the real photos yourself. We would rather be honest about an
        image than impressive with one.
      </p>
      <h2>Say hello</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or a tiny room you are proud of? Write to us at
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a> or use the
        <a href="/contact"> contact page</a>. We read everything.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="mt-12 flex items-start gap-4 rounded-3xl border border-sand bg-beige/60 p-6">
      <span class="flex h-14 w-14 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-terracotta font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">SN</span>
      <div>
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">The {siteConfig.publisher.authorName}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cocoa">{siteConfig.publisher.authorBio}</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
